{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650923,"nonce":"jX4VGFrG+8pj2BBpcLDZ0/30P90=","title":"Mandible Tauri: Level 2 self-contained app (bundled daemon sidecar)","message":"Make the Mandible.app self-contained so it starts the daemon itself on launch, with no dependency on dotfiles session hooks.\n\nSteps:\n1. Compile the Node.js daemon to a standalone binary (bun build --compile or pkg)\n2. Add it as a Tauri sidecar in tauri.conf.json under bundle.externalBin\n3. In lib.rs: spawn sidecar on startup, poll localhost:19420 until ready, then show window\n\nCurrently Level 1 (thin launcher) is implemented: the app opens a window at localhost:19420 but requires the daemon to already be running.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue bf366d8.","files":null}]}